1
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
There's a world on both sides of the rainbow where songs come true
and every time it rains, it rains Pennies from Heaven.

2
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Pennies from Heaven is a drama, music, romance film directed by Herbert Ross.

3
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
During the Great Depression, a sheet music salesman seeks to escape his dreary life
through popular music and a love affair with an innocent schoolteacher.

4
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Arthur, played by Steve Martin.

5
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Eileen, played by Bernadette Peters.

6
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Joan, played by Jessica Harper.

7
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
The Accordion Man, played by Vernel Bagneris.

8
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Mr. Warner, played by John McMartin.

9
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The Detective, played by John Karlen.

10
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Pennies from Heaven is a 1981 American musical romantic drama film directed
by Herbert Ross, based on the 1978 BBC television drama.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Dennis Potter adapted his screenplay from the BBC series for American audiences, changing its
setting from London and the Forest of Dean to Depression-era Chicago and rural Illinois.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film stars Steve Martin, Bernadette Peters,
Christopher Walken and Jessica Harper.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Choreographed by Danny Daniels, the film includes musical numbers consisting of actors lip-syncing and dancing to popular songs of the
1920s–30s, such as "Let's Misbehave", "Life Is Just a Bowl of Cherries", "Let's Face the Music and Dance" and the title song.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
While positively received by critics, it was a box office
bomb, grossing just a fraction of its budget.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
It received 3 nominations at the 54th Academy
Awards, but didn't win any of them.

16
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
The film explores themes of chicago, illinois,
marriage, musical, great depression, teacher.

17
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
The tone is emotional.
